                    <birth when="0000-00-00">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1824"/>
                    <occupation>Medical Officer, Medical Sceptic</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Charles Maclean was a Scottish medical officer stationed with the East
                            India Company from 1788 on ships, before being stationed on the
                            continent. However, his sceptical views on vaccination and quarantine
                            resulted in regular dismissal from the different positions he held
                            throughout his career. He published works discrediting the effectivness
                            of vaccination and quarantine as goernment policy, such as 'On the State
                            of Vaccnination in 1810' and 'Practical Illusions of the Progress of
                            Medical Improvement'. References to him in the diaries coincide with a
                            period in which his travel to Spain was disrupted as a result of the
                            ongoing war. Godwin does not record his death in 1824</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="MS"> </bibl>
